  "selection": "Five new policies crossing original mixed/local/navigation features and greedy/expected TD targets, excluding the unchanged incumbent from candidates. Prefer cue-component retention plus nonnegative mean population differences against frozen, noMemory, neural and incumbent in BOTH environments, stable mean energy >= -0.5 versus incumbent, and positive relocation mean energy versus incumbent. Rank by the worst mean energy difference across stable/relocation frozen, noMemory and neural comparisons plus relocation against incumbent; tie by ID. Lock one policy before opening held-out data. If no development candidate is eligible, evaluate the top exploratory candidate without reselection or promotion.",
  "interpretation": "Human-designed experiment motivated by post-hoc same-seed action forks and retrieval-distance observations, not evidence those observations establish a cause. Navigation features exclude clock/mate/age while keeping energy and bias; local features additionally exclude energy/bias. Expected targets use the actual configured epsilon-greedy action distribution, not a no-exploration future. Matched founders, fixed body/food/energy prices, same memory bound and lookups. No reproduction/mutation or environmental promotion. Qualification requires positive energy lower bound and nonnegative population mean versus all four required controls in BOTH worlds, stable incumbent noninferiority (-0.5 energy lower bound), positive relocation advantage over incumbent with no mean population loss, and the separate underlying cue-memory component. The cue task does not exercise TD bootstrapping or prove whole-body continual retention. Relevant feature/target ablations are secondary; do not attribute independent component benefit unless their intervals support it.",
